Publish native GMAC offload features before registering the NSS-DP netdev.

DSA copies vlan_features when it creates user ports, which can happen
before the conduit is opened. Publishing the features only at open leaves
those ports without scatter-gather and prevents Linux from enabling their
software GSO.

For the native IPQ5018 phylink path, publish the host dataplane features at
probe. NSS supports the same checksum, scatter-gather and fraglist features,
so the initial DSA capabilities are valid across takeover and host restore.

--- a/nss_dp_main.c
+++ b/nss_dp_main.c
@@ -1004,7 +1004,12 @@ static int nss_dp_probe(struct platform_
 	}
 #endif
 
-	/* TODO: Features: CSUM, tx/rx offload... configure */
+	/*
+	 * DSA user ports inherit the conduit's VLAN features before it opens.
+	 * Publish the native IPQ5018 features shared by the NSS dataplane.
+	 */
+	if (dp_priv->ipq5018)
+		dp_priv->data_plane_ops->set_features(dp_priv->dpc);
 
 	/* Register the network interface */
 	ret = register_netdev(netdev);
